lyric_anchors.text:
[Intro]
Told Tesla I know why you Talk to that Itty Bitty Bird;
Sat on the Bench and Threw some Bread, thinking about everything I Heard.

[Verse 1]
Itty Bitty Birdy said what Matters is the Matter that frequents the Seas,
Going hum, drum, fee, fi, fo, Zee-zummm… 
The Birds brought a Plum from the Tree for the Bees;
Three. Six. Nine.  Some 90s rapper said damn she Fine; 
Goes through Me, yours, and forever formally never-never Mine…

Hozier told me to go to Church, but I preferred the Shrike;
She came in like Tesla’s bird on her Motorbike.
Maybe Work Song will get me on that Hike, Hike Hike…

Our Anima… It’s an Ocean of our Wins;
Closed my eyes and went with Tidus and Yuna to go fight Sin’s;
Kissed the goccia di kopi sulla tua pancia,
When we stole a night before the end of the last Parapancha.

[Pre-chorus]
Years passed since I met Vita,
Met in April after a March of his to a Bridge;

Take these Seeds I got from the “Maybe.”
And if you see my Grand Mother,
Toss a Coin to Wish her Well;
I’ll Catch Two in my Eye
And Wake Up where they Fell;

[Verse 1]
I went Paddle Boarding with a Pisces wearing a One Piece Flag;
Said Captain pass the Roach with the Witcher signs to the Yuffy dressed in Drag;
Roach is a Work-Shrek walking towards a Princess carrying a Donkey;
Walked Right through Bali and picked up Mon-Chi-Chi, 
Said we’re going back to Kick it at a Mon-key-key;
But we should set our Sails before the Sun sets her’s,
Because that Moon is A Harsh one, Mister,
And the Going is Good Now to Protect our Sister;
